  "content": "Dreaming feature (shipped 2026-05-26): the MCP client pushes conversation turns via record_messages into the session_messages table (local-only, never sync'd). On a schedule or via dream_now / the desktop button, the reasoner reviews messages + recent memories and returns a JSON ops list (create/update/delete with a required `reasoning` field). Foreground dreams prefer sampling; background scheduled dreams need a direct reasoner (no session for sampling). A planned integration point for calling record_messages on each conversation turn exists but is not currently invoked by Claude Code. Single-flight via dreamMu.TryLock() - concurrent dreams return Skipped=true. The judge feature is planned next: a layer where new memories go through human or LLM rating; config will let user pick which.",
  "tags": [
    "dreaming",
    "judge",
    "roadmap"
  ],
